{
  "id": "v08_key_not_retained",
  "title": "A receipt whose retired key is no longer published",
  "test_plan_vector": null,
  "spec": [
    "Platform Verification 1: MUST verify each receipt's signature against the `keys` of the business named in `iss`. A receipt whose `typ` is not `ucp-ap2-receipt+jwt`, or whose `kid` does not resolve in the `keys` of `iss`, is `receipt_invalid_signature`.",
    "Platform Verification 3: MUST exclude a receipt that fails rule 1 or 2 from its chain, so the next receipt in that chain is reported as `receipt_sequence_gap`.",
    "Platform Verification 4: MUST evaluate `seq` and `prev` continuity per `(iss, mandate_ref)` chain. A second, different receipt for a `seq` the platform already holds is `receipt_sequence_gap`; the platform keeps both.",
    "Business Requirements 9: MUST keep retired public keys resolvable by `kid` for at least the dispute window of the payment method used."
  ],
  "signing": "TEST-ONLY P-256 keys derived from fixed labels in common/payments/ap2_receipt_fixtures.py; deterministic ECDSA (RFC 6979). Never use them outside these vectors.",
  "notes": "Negative counterpart of v08_rotated_retained_key: test_only_2025 is gone from keys, so the `kid` of seq 1 does not resolve and it is receipt_invalid_signature. It is then excluded from the chain, so seq 2 is reported as a gap and, because the totals are recomputed without the excluded receipt, as a totals mismatch too (see v06_missing_seq).",
